  "content": {
    "id": "p5-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "A triangle has sides of length 5, 6 and 7.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p5-q13-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the length of its longest altitude, as shown below. (Note that an altitude is a line segment drawn from a vertex of a triangle that meets the opposing side at a right angle.)",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [
          {
            "id": "p5-q13-diagram",
            "role": "question",
            "format": "tikz",
            "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"source page 5 p5-q13-diagram\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.65cm,y=0.65cm,every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,text=black}]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\coordinate (L) at (0,0);\\coordinate (R) at (5,0);\\coordinate (T) at (1.2,5.878775383);\\coordinate (F) at (1.2,0);\n\\draw[line width=0.8pt] (L)--(T)--(R)--cycle;\n\\draw[line width=0.4pt] (T)--(F);\n\\draw[line width=0.4pt] (1.2,0.3)--(1.5,0.3)--(1.5,0);\n\\path (L)--(T) node[midway,left] {$6$};\\path (T)--(R) node[midway,right] {$7$};\\path (L)--(R) node[midway,below] {$5$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
            "src": null,
            "widthMm": 31.6,
            "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
            "overlayOf": null,
            "transparent": false,
            "axes": null,
            "spec": {
              "sourcePage": 5,
              "sourceRegion": "Question 13(a)",
              "description": "Unfilled triangle with base 5, left side 6, right side 7 and an unlabelled perpendicular altitude. Decorative cyan fill omitted under house style.",
              "mathematics": "Coordinates give side lengths 5, 6 and 7 exactly; altitude foot is 6/5 from the left endpoint.",
              "answerVisibility": "Only source givens are visible; altitude length is not supplied."
            },
            "derived": false,
            "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
          }
        ],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{12\\sqrt6}{5}$ units.\n\nThe longest altitude meets the shortest side, of length 5.",
          "worked": "Let the altitude be $h$ and the left base segment be $x$. The right base segment is $5-x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}h^2+x^2&=36\\\\h^2+(5-x)^2&=49\\\\(5-x)^2-x^2&=13\\\\25-10x&=13\\\\x&=\\frac65\\\\h^2&=36-\\left(\\frac65\\right)^2\\\\h^2&=\\frac{864}{25}\\\\h&=\\frac{12\\sqrt6}{5}\\end{align*}$$\nFor fixed area, the altitude is largest when its base is shortest.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 96
      },
      {
        "id": "p5-q13-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, find the area of the triangle.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$6\\sqrt6$ square units.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\frac12bh\\\\A&=\\frac12\\times5\\times\\frac{12\\sqrt6}{5}\\\\A&=6\\sqrt6\\end{align*}$$\nThe area is $6\\sqrt6$ square units.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p5-q13-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Hence, find the length of its shortest altitude.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{12\\sqrt6}{7}$ units.\n\nUse the longest side, 7, as the base.",
          "worked": "The shortest altitude meets the longest side. Let this altitude be $k$.\n$$\\begin{align*}6\\sqrt6&=\\frac12\\times7\\times k\\\\k&=\\frac{2\\times6\\sqrt6}{7}\\\\k&=\\frac{12\\sqrt6}{7}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      }
    ]
  },
